# H-IU1 directed A/B for D-IUNLINK-PREV-OF-PEER-FREED-INODE-STALE-PRECOMMIT-
# SHUTDOWN on 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e (test17 test18).  Same build for both arms:
# ~/src/mxfs-c srcversion D2472E4A4BED5A6D8DC8AF8, the main tree's sources with
# H-IU1 in (module knob unlprev_held_verify: 1 = under the predecessor's EX
# hold, a predecessor that is no longer live, unlinked and pointing at the
# inode being freed clears that inode's prev pointer and starts the free over,
# so the preflight rebuilds the chain from the platter; 0 = the same-build
# control that removes with the stale pointer).  The check, its P-UNLPREV-MOVED
# line and the unlprev_held_moved count run in both settings.  Run from
# ~/src/mxfs-c.
#
# WHY DIRECTED (written before the first lap).  The random noino_gen0 workload
# (tests/queues/unlprev_verify_ab_mpath.queue, laps iub1-3) held 10-66
# predecessor waits open 300 ms each and no predecessor was freed inside one:
# moved=0 on every lap.  tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh makes the window on
# every iteration: the owner removes z and then y, which the peer holds open,
# so y heads the owner's bucket ahead of z, and closes z.  z's free finds y in
# core, cancels, drops the AG DLM and asks for y's EX hold (P-UNLPREV-WAIT);
# with dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500 it asks only after PUC_HOLD_S=3 has run
# out and the peer's last close of y has taken y off the list and freed it --
# fn32's sequence on the owner's own bucket.  PUC_RESET_AFTER sets the delay
# back to 0 before the settle and the cold audit.  Ten iterations per lap.
#
# HYPOTHESIS H-IU1 (in the record before the patch): when xfs_inactive_ifree
# drops the AG DLM to take its predecessor's EX hold, the predecessor's owner
# can take it off the list and free it in that gap; the retry trusts the freed
# inode's in-core i_prev_unlinked without re-checking it under the hold, so
# xfs_iunlink_remove_inode edits a free inode's next pointer, the precommit
# finds NULLAGINO where it expects the inode being freed, and the commit shuts
# the filesystem down.
#
# READING RULES (written before the first lap):
#   Reach is held_moved (unlprev_held_moved summed over the nodes) with a
#   moved_freed count above zero on some node's MOVED lines (a held
#   predecessor read back free).  A lap without reach counts for neither arm.
#   SUPPORTED when at least one control lap is REPRODUCED with sig_iu1 > 0 (a
#   P53-IUNLINK-MISMATCH on an inode a P-UNLPREV-MOVED line of the same node
#   named as the held predecessor) and that node's shutdown follows it, and
#   every fix lap with reach is PASS with rebuilds > 0, no P53 mismatch and no
#   node failure, with at least three fix laps reaching.
#   REFUTED if a fix lap shows a P53 mismatch followed by a shutdown on a remove
#   whose held predecessor passed the check, or if every control lap with
#   moved_freed > 0 ends without a P53 mismatch (the stale pointer then does
#   not lead to the shutdown).
#   Otherwise undecided: more laps on the same rules, never a disposition.
#   Any other failure (P-UNLREM-NOPREV, P-UNLREM-BACKREF, an ifree error no
#   MOVED line explains, a hang, the deferred-free shutdown
#   P-IFREE-DEFER-UNLANDED-FATAL) is attributed from its own lines to its own
#   record before anything else.  A fix lap's frees that ran out of tries defer
#   to the reaper; their count is P-UNLPREV-REBUILD lines with try=4.
#
# Bound per lap: tests/queues/peer_open_unlinked_hu6_census.queue's 2437 s
# less 20 iterations of that harness's 11 s workload budget (220 s) and five
# of its knobs at 2 x 20 s (200 s), plus one PUC_RESET_AFTER knob reset at
# 2 x 20 s: 2057 s.  The 4.5 s delay sits inside one iteration's 11 s budget
# (the close of z waits for it; the peer's hold is 3 s).
2057 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_HOLD_S=3 PUC_KNOBS="unlprev_held_verify=0 dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500" PUC_RESET_AFTER=dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh iud1 10 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e
2057 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_HOLD_S=3 PUC_KNOBS="unlprev_held_verify=1 dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500" PUC_RESET_AFTER=dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh iud2 10 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e
2057 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_HOLD_S=3 PUC_KNOBS="unlprev_held_verify=0 dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500" PUC_RESET_AFTER=dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh iud3 10 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e
2057 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_HOLD_S=3 PUC_KNOBS="unlprev_held_verify=1 dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500" PUC_RESET_AFTER=dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh iud4 10 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e
2057 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_HOLD_S=3 PUC_KNOBS="unlprev_held_verify=1 dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500" PUC_RESET_AFTER=dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh iud5 10 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e
2057 MXFS_SNAPSHOT_DIR=/mxfs/snapshots PUC_HOLD_S=3 PUC_KNOBS="unlprev_held_verify=0 dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms=4500" PUC_RESET_AFTER=dbg_unlprev_wait_delay_ms tests/peer_open_unlinked_chain.sh iud6 10 2/net/mesh/mpath g2e
